--
-- PostGIS types without binary send/recv in versioned tables: raster and
-- spheroid are kept as their text forms and come back byte-identical
-- through commits, moves and merges, alone and in arrays, domains and
-- composites; box2d and box3d values whose text doesn't read back the same
-- are refused where they're written, never at a commit; box2df and gidx,
-- index keys, can hold no value.  And a NaN point comes back from a
-- commit as POINT EMPTY, as through pg_dump: its EWKB is an empty
-- point's.
--
\set ECHO none
on main|t
without send/recv|box2d,box2df,box3d,gidx,raster,spheroid
status|public.gis_nosend new table
commit|t
reset|t
reset: same|t
reset: raster reads|7,3.6666667461395264,1.5
branch|t
commit main|t
checkout|t
checkout: same|t
commit side|t
merge|{0,0,"merge successful"}
merged|1:5:true:BOX(0 0,1 1),6:3.6666667461395264:false:BOX(2 2,3 3),7:1.5:false:BOX(0 0,1 1)
checkout main|t
extent refused|0A000 value of type box2d can't be stored in a versioned table: its text form doesn't read back as the same value
extent 3D|accepted
status after|1
box2df value|0A000 function box2df_in not implemented
gidx value|0A000 function gidx_in not implemented
nulls commit|t
before|1:false:0101000000000000000000f87f000000000000f87f,2:false:0101000000000000000000f8ff000000000000f8ff,3:true:0101000000000000000000f87f000000000000f87f,4:false:0101000000000000000000f03f0000000000000040
commit nan|t
reset|t
after|1:true:0101000000000000000000f87f000000000000f87f,2:true:0101000000000000000000f87f000000000000f87f,3:true:0101000000000000000000f87f000000000000f87f,4:false:0101000000000000000000f03f0000000000000040
strict bbox|t
commit strict|t
reset strict|t
strict after|t
strict reads|1:1,2:4,3:2,4:-1,5:1
strict bbox after|f
beside refused|added:2
refused alone|0
pages base|t
pages refused key|t
pages rows|51|2375
